Subject: marc_root: link the arena's root modules before the root mounts

30 section 3, section 2 patch 16's root half (S4-04), contract C4-4
section 4.  dlm_marc_root(), the kernel's hook in rth1_mountroot before
rth1_apply, walks the arena directory in order in no-sleep mode (level 7,
the clock stopped, U1).  Each entry's CRC-32 is taken again: bytes that
changed after boot2 checked them are not linked.  The manifest copy must
hold a root record of that name and crc32=, and gives its bss=.  Then
dlm_load_mem.  ENXIO (no such board) is silent, any other error one line.
In safe mode only the safe-mode members (flag 0x4) link.  dlm_arena_init
keeps the arena's address; dlm_crc32 gives the core the loader's CRC-32.
A file off 16 in the arena now has its own line (it shared the bss
one in 0033).  The state harness builds arenas as boot2 does and checks
each case.

